<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chaldaei</span></b> , ōrum,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χαλδαῖοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the
			Chaldœans</i>, <i>a people of Assyria</i>,
				<i>distinguished</i>, <i>in an early
				age</i>, <i>for their knowledge of astronomy and
				astrology.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of <i>the
				nation</i> or <i>people</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 28,
				32, § 105</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 8,
			5</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			gen., <i>soothsayers</i>, <i>astrologers</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Div. 1, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 42,
			87</span></i> sq.; <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 3, 1, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 14,
				1, 1</span></i> sqq.; sing.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chaldaeus,</span>”
				<i>a soothsayer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 5, 4</span></i>
			; <i>gen. plur.</i> Chaldaeūm, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
			726</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chaldaeus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>Chaldœan</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">regnum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Luc.
					8, 226</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Esp.,
				<i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
				soothsayers</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 25, 57, § 211</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">grex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 94</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Chal-dăĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">genus praedicendi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 42, 88</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 47, 98</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 26, 30, § 121</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
